        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF156 adds support for the async Clipboard API to use web custom formats.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The  API allows you to create a <code class=\"notranslate\">ClipboardItem</code> that contains several representations of a copied object, such as version in HTML and Text, and push it to the system clipboard. Something else can read the clipboard and get back tha object - then choose the best format it understands.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The update allows you to (behind a pref) use other types than PNG, HTML, txt.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What this update does is make the model above clear, because it wasn't - it referred too much to \"arbitrary types\" can didn't capture \"different representations\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the first part of the job. After this I'll do the custom web formats bit.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5312307167\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45430\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45430/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45430\">#45430</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45620",
            "title": "FF156 ClipBoard Async API - clarify types",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-11T07:09:41.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-11T07:07:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43131.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3941254411\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43131\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43131/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43131\">#43131</a>. Note that Firefox seems to behave differently but not sure if it merits a note.</p>",
